# TENANT-STORAGE-MODE-GATE (Tenant Storage Mode Compatibility Gate)

**Related:** `<DEC-TENANCY>` (e.g. platform/tenant separation), tenant storage resolver contract, auth-model boundary report, INTEGRITY verification section.

**Portable template** — replace project paths, DEC refs, model/trait names, and allowlist sources after copy to `<project>/.cursor/rules/`.

```yaml
tenant_storage_mode_gate:
  Pattern_to_KSS_Template: approved
  portable_structure: true
  project_content: replace_required
```

## Step 0 — Trigger evaluation (required first)

This rule is available for all plans, but **applies only when scope matches** the trigger below.

**Trigger scope** — plan touches any of:

- tenant-facing surfaces (routes, controllers, pages, API)
- tenant-data models or migrations
- tenant-auth, tenant-session, tenant-settings, tenant-security
- tenant programmatic API / tokens

**If trigger does NOT match:** record in the plan:

```text
## Storage Mode Compatibility (PRV)
**Status:** Not applicable — plan scope does not touch tenant storage modes.
```

Then skip all requirements below. Do **not** burden unrelated plans.

**If trigger matches:** complete the full PRV section before executing plan todos.

---

## Two-tier compatibility model

| Tier | Artifacts | `shared_db` | `database_per_tenant` | `schema_per_tenant` |
|------|-----------|-------------|----------------------|---------------------|
| **Auth / Security / Session / API** | Tenant user, membership, MFA, RBAC, tokens, sessions, security policies | Required | Required | Statement: deferred / not touched |
| **Domain operational** | Domain models intentionally on shared per auth-model boundary | Required | **Deferred** per project boundary doc | Statement required |

Domain-tier artifacts without storage resolver trait are **not** automatic defects when documented as domain-on-shared.

---

## Mandatory plan section (when triggered)

Every triggered plan MUST include:

```markdown
## Storage Mode Compatibility (PRV)

| Check | shared_db | database_per_tenant | schema_per_tenant |
|-------|-----------|---------------------|-------------------|
| Tier (auth/security vs domain) | auth / domain | auth / domain | deferred / not touched |
| Models: storage resolver trait | yes/no/na | yes/no/na | na |
| BelongsToTenant when usesExplicitTenantIdColumn | yes/no/na | yes/no/na | na |
| Tests attested (class names) | ... | ... | deferred |
| Raw DB::connection('tenant') in services | none / allowlist ref | none / allowlist ref | n/a |
| Central reads for tenant runtime data | none | none | n/a |
| Hardcoded shared-tenant DB assumption | none | none | n/a |
```

**Stop condition:** PRV incomplete or unverifiable → **do NOT execute** plan todos.

---

## Rules (when triggered)

| Rule | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| Resolver | Use project tenant storage resolver + model connection trait; never assume a fixed shared physical DB name |
| Services | No `DB::connection('tenant')` in module services except rows in INTEGRITY allowlist (owner-accepted, closure-report sourced) |
| Central reads | No central DB reads for tenant runtime data (registry exceptions: tenant registry, domains, provisioning metadata) |
| BelongsToTenant | Apply only when `usesExplicitTenantIdColumn()` is true for the tenant |
| schema_per_tenant | Explicit row: `tested` / `deferred` / `not touched` |
| Domain tier | Reference auth-model boundary doc when deferring dedicated storage |

---

## Allowlist discipline

No vague “approved allowlist.” Each `DB::connection('tenant')` exception in INTEGRITY_RULES must trace to a closure-report row with: exact file/method, reason, tier, risk, expiry/follow-up backlog item, owner acceptance.

---

## Plan preflight cross-reference

When `plan-preflight-gate` triggers on tenancy/database/security, this gate also applies. Complete PRV before todos.
